    "rationale": "The serving chain gates on predict_proba at 0.55: at or above the gate the domain is fixed and Sarvam-30B only resolves the leaf; below it the LLM does zero-shot over the whole taxonomy. A family exposing only decision_function cannot drive that gate, which rules out LinearSVC (C=1.0, balanced), RidgeClassifier (balanced) regardless of score. OPEN FINDING \u2014 the incumbent is not the strongest probability-capable family on this split: SGDClassifier (modified_huber, balanced) scores 0.988 vs the incumbent's 0.9824 (+0.0056 val macro-F1). This is recorded, not acted on. A swap is not a drop-in: modified_huber probabilities come from a clipped decision function and are materially less well-calibrated than logistic ones, and the entire confidence gate, the Green/Yellow/Red bands and the drift monitor's low-confidence alerts are all calibration-dependent. Adopting it requires re-running the gate calibration and the CI behavioural gate first."
